# Virtual environments
.venv/
**/.venv/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store
._*

# ─── Heavy local data / generated outputs ────────────────────────
# Bake outputs (the simulators dump MP4 / GIF playbacks here).
# ``**/bakes/`` covers nested per-sim bakes folders.
Baked_Playbacks/
bakes/
**/bakes/
example-playback-csv/
tile_cache/

# Generated media. The simulators write benchmark GIFs / preview
# MP4s into result directories during dev — they're hundreds of MB
# of regenerable artifacts, never useful in git history.
*.mp4
*.gif
**/benchmark_results/

# Ad-hoc test / script outputs (per-experiment images next to the
# script that produced them).
**/scripts/test_*.png
**/scripts/test_*.gif

# Per-run empirical-results dumps (CSVs are kept — they're the
# source of truth; PNG renders next to them are regenerable).
**/data/empirical_results/*.png

# Terrain cache files. lidar_sim_gui.py ray-casts the STL once and
# saves a 16-bit ``*.terrain.png`` / ``*.test_terrain.png`` next to
# it as a precomputed elevation/shading cache; subsequent runs load
# instantly. Regenerated on demand whenever the cache is missing
# or older than the STL. The default-STL cache
# (``Lidar_Surface_fast.terrain.png``, ~386 KB) is checked in so a
# fresh clone doesn't have to pay the one-time bake cost; all other
# variants stay out of git.
**/3d_assets/*.terrain.png
**/3d_assets/*.test_terrain.png
!LiDAR Sim/3d_assets/Lidar_Surface_fast.terrain.png

# ROS bag recordings. The GUI sim's recording mode dumps a
# ``manual_<timestamp>/`` directory per session containing a 280+ MB
# ``.db3`` SQLite bag, plus camera/lidar/costmap captures. These are
# session artifacts, never source-of-truth.
*.bag
*.db3
*.mcap
**/bag/metadata.yaml

# NumPy serialised arrays. The LiDAR sim writes ``*.npy`` /
# ``*.npz`` cache files next to STLs (e.g. ``*.spawn_mask.npy``,
# ``*_costmap.npz``) and inside ``data/manual_*/`` recording dirs.
# All are regenerable on demand.
*.npy
*.npz

# ``generate_grade_map.py`` defaults its PNG outputs into the script
# directory. List the known output names so they don't accidentally
# slip in alongside source.
**/scripts/grade_map.png
**/scripts/slope_raw.png
**/scripts/slope_*.png

# Whole GUI Sim recording-session folders. Match anything under a
# ``manual_<...>/`` directory inside ``GUI Sim/data/`` (the recorder
# names them with a timestamp). Catches everything the recorder
# writes per session in one rule.
GUI Sim/data/manual_*/
**/data/manual_*/

# Blender autosave backups
*.blend1

# Editor / Claude local state
.claude/settings.local.json
